# Cloudflare Pages headers. Mirrors the `headers` block in vercel.json.
#
# Syntax note: this is NOT regex. Pages matches literal paths with `*` splats
# and `:placeholders`, so the `/(audio|figure)/(.*)` form vercel.json uses has
# to become one rule per prefix. Every matching rule applies, so the security
# headers under /* land on the hashed assets too rather than being overridden.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Vite hashes these filenames, and the audio and sprite names are stable and
# only ever added to, so a year is safe on all three.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/audio/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/figure/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
